\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Exact ledger for the frozen ordered moduli $q=2,3,5,7,11,4,6,9,10$. (A) The cyclic locus can be smaller than the exact-order shell, but its cardinality always equals $|C_q|$ in the registered audit. (B) Full-centralizer, symplectic-centralizer, and cyclic-$A$-orbit counts are kept distinct. (C) The full cyclic quotient has one class at every control; the symplectic cyclic quotient has the exact norm-image count, and full-shell quotients expose the additional split/ramified strata. Reversing groups were audited only at the five prime controls, so composite entries are marked not audited. These development-seen finite rows verify the implementation and fixed controls; they do not prove the all-$q$ formulas.}}{9}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:nine-modulus-ledger}{{2}{9}{Exact ledger for the frozen ordered moduli $q=2,3,5,7,11,4,6,9,10$. (A) The cyclic locus can be smaller than the exact-order shell, but its cardinality always equals $|C_q|$ in the registered audit. (B) Full-centralizer, symplectic-centralizer, and cyclic-$A$-orbit counts are kept distinct. (C) The full cyclic quotient has one class at every control; the symplectic cyclic quotient has the exact norm-image count, and full-shell quotients expose the additional split/ramified strata. Reversing groups were audited only at the five prime controls, so composite entries are marked not audited. These development-seen finite rows verify the implementation and fixed controls; they do not prove the all-$q$ formulas}{figure.2}{}}
\newlabel{eq:observed-norm-classes}{{37}{9}{Registered nine-modulus ledger}{equation.6.37}{}}
